      "explanation": "<p> Primary amine reacts in presence of chloroform gives isonitrile which is toxic in nature which further reacts in presence of HCl/H<sub>3</sub>O<sup>+</sup> to give primary amine and acid.</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l2pjg0y6/53c9b964-73e1-4bf1-b1e1-e7d266d7b6de/b0159ee0-ca89-11ec-ab2b-7960e659c3b6/file-1l2pjg0y7.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l2pjg0y6/53c9b964-73e1-4bf1-b1e1-e7d266d7b6de/b0159ee0-ca89-11ec-ab2b-7960e659c3b6/file-1l2pjg0y7.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 20th July Morning Shift Chemistry - Compounds Containing Nitrogen Question 166 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l2pjg0y6/53c9b964-73e1-4bf1-b1e1-e7d266d7b6de/b0159ee0-ca89-11ec-ab2b-7960e659c3b6/file-1l2pjg0y7.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l2pjg0y6/53c9b964-73e1-4bf1-b1e1-e7d266d7b6de/b0159ee0-ca89-11ec-ab2b-7960e659c3b6/file-1l2pjg0y7.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l2pjg0y6/53c9b964-73e1-4bf1-b1e1-e7d266d7b6de/b0159ee0-ca89-11ec-ab2b-7960e659c3b6/file-1l2pjg0y7.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l2pjg0y6/53c9b964-73e1-4bf1-b1e1-e7d266d7b6de/b0159ee0-ca89-11ec-ab2b-7960e659c3b6/file-1l2pjg0y7.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l2pjg0y6/53c9b964-73e1-4bf1-b1e1-e7d266d7b6de/b0159ee0-ca89-11ec-ab2b-7960e659c3b6/file-1l2pjg0y7.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l2pjg0y6/53c9b964-73e1-4bf1-b1e1-e7d266d7b6de/b0159ee0-ca89-11ec-ab2b-7960e659c3b6/file-1l2pjg0y7.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Hence, A-primary amine, B-isonitrile compound and C-conc. HCl.</p>"
